^SERIES = GSE210152
!Series_title = Single cell immune landscape of human atherosclerosis reveals the transcriptional signature of PLIN2hi/TREM1hi inflammatory lipid-associated macrophages and its association with cerebrovascular complications.
!Series_geo_accession = GSE210152
!Series_status = Public on May 22 2023
!Series_submission_date = Jul 31 2022
!Series_last_update_date = Jun 10 2026
!Series_pubmed_id = 38362263
!Series_summary = Atherosclerosis is a lipid-driven inflammatory disease.However, evidence emerging so far from single cell atlases suggests a dichotomy between lipid associated and inflammatory macrophage states. Here, we present the most inclusive reference atlas of human intraplaque immune cell communities to date.
!Series_overall_design = Carotid plaques were collected from patients undergoing carotid endarterectomy. Tissues were enzymatically digested, and single cells were sorted for CD45+ cells.
!Series_overall_design = CD45+ single cell suspensions were processed using the 10x Genomics platform with the aim to capture 5,000 cells/sample. 
!Series_overall_design = Update 10/6/26: Patients P1, P2, P6 and P7 were symptomatic (GSM6422822, GSM6422823, GSM6422826, GSM6422827). Patients P3 and P5 were asymptomatic (GSM6422824, GSM6422825).
!Series_type = Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing
